  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Raju Vachunuri S/O. Vachunuri Raja ... vs State Of Maharashtra on 14 September, 2022 Author: Nitin W. Sambre Bench: Nitin W. Sambre 906_ABA2518_22.doc In The High Court Of Judicature At Bombay Criminal Appellate Jurisdiction Anticipatory Bail Application No.2518 Of 2022 Krishnamurari @ Kallu Rajendra Gupta ... Applicant Vs. State of Maharashtra ... Respondent And Anticipatory Bail Application No.2519 Of 2022 Raju Vachunuri s/o Vachunuri Raja Komaraiah ... Applicant Vs. State of Maharashtra ... Respondent Mr. Pranav P. Pokale a/w. Mr. Nikhil Patwa, Mr. Tanmay Karwa and Mr.Aditya Bagal for Applicants in both the Applications. Mr. N. B. Patil, App for Respondent-State in Aba/2518/2022. Ms. P. N. Dabholkar, App for Respondent-State in Aba/2519/2022. Mr. S. J. Patil, Police Constable, Lonavala City Police Station. Coram : Nitin W. Sambre, J. Date : September 14, 2022 P.C. : Heard. 2. The applicant - Krishnamurari @ Kallu Rajendra Gupta is seeking pre-arrest bail in Crime No.926 of 2021 registered with Chakan Police Station, Pune for the offences punishable under Sections 328, 272, 273, 188 and 34 of the Ipc. 3. The applicant - Raju Vachunuri s/o Vachunuri Raja Komaraiah is seeking pre-arrest bail in Crime No.19 of 2022 registered with Lonavala City Police Station, Pune (Rural) for the offences punishable under Sections 328, 188 and 34 of the Ipc as also Sections 26(2), 26(2) (a), 27(3)(d), 27(3)(e) and 59 of the Food Safety and Standards Act, 2006. 3. Whether the provisions of Section 328 of the Ipc are applicable in the facts of the present case is an issue subjudice before the Apex 906_ABA2518_22.doc Court.",
